            <div xml:id="d918">

                <pb facs="0789" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/2643: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-11T10:00:00-05:00">September 11, 1940—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. Department’s telegram No. 140, August 30, 5 p.m.<anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d918-f1"/> The Secretary of the Treasury has just informed me that
                    instead of a $15,000,000 loan the Government now wants a $65,000,000 loan and
                    that a detailed request will be forwarded to Washington promptly. He of course
                    does not favor the loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
